<Layout title="About & Education — Cain Macias" description="Explore Cain Macias’s background, degrees in computer science, business analytics and healthcare administration, and professional certifications."><header class="ref-page-intro ref-reveal">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">About Me</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
      I work across software engineering, business systems, and business analysis in Corpus Christi, Texas. My work centers on bridging complex legacy enterprise architectures with modern automation, data pipelines, and intelligent agents.
    </p>
    <a class="about-linkedin" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/cain-macias-a69801306/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Connect on LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </header>

  <div class="ref-about-content">
    <section class="ref-about-timeline ref-reveal" aria-labelledby="timeline-title">
      <div class="ref-section-label"><span class="ref-label-line"></span> TIMELINE <span class="ref-label-right">WORK & EDUCATION</span></div>
      <h2 id="timeline-title">where I've been</h2>
      <ol class="ref-timeline-list">
        <li>
          <div class="ref-timeline-dot ref-timeline-dot-mint"></div>
          <div class="ref-timeline-entry"><div class="ref-timeline-title"><strong>Jean's Restaurant Supply (Tari, Inc.)</strong><span>2025 — Now</span></div><p>Software Engineer · Enterprise systems, automation, and integration engineering</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="ref-timeline-dot ref-timeline-dot-blue"></div>
          <div class="ref-timeline-entry"><div class="ref-timeline-title"><strong>CHRISTUS Health</strong><span>2023 — 2025</span></div><p>Medical Laboratory Technician II · Data quality, precision, and clinical workflows</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div class="ref-timeline-dot ref-timeline-dot-gold"></div>
          <div class="ref-timeline-entry"><div class="ref-timeline-title"><strong>Schlitterbahn</strong><span>2018 — 2022</span></div><p>Warehouse Operations Supervisor · Inventory, reporting, and process improvements</p></div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">The Journey</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        As a first-generation college graduate and the oldest of four, my path into technology wasn't linear. Growing up, I didn't have a roadmap or easy access to technical mentors. After facing the loss of my Father right before my 15th birthday, I had to learn how to navigate academic hurdles—moving through aviation mechanics, pre-med biology, and remedial coursework before discovering my footing in Medical Laboratory Technology.
      </p>
      <p>
        Working as a Medical Lab Technician at Christus Health taught me the absolute value of precision, data integrity, and root-cause analysis. It was also where a mentor recognized my potential to look beyond individual testing errors and understand how entire operational systems function.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Transitioning to Systems & Software</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Technology has been a lifelong curiosity whether building custom home servers, experimenting with Linux distributions, or modding games. When I realized that software and automation offered an even larger canvas for root cause analysis and systemic problem solving, I dove in headfirst. As an early adopter of AI tooling starting in 2023, I began engineering pipelines that turned manual bottlenecks into autonomous workflows.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today, my goal is simple: to build resilient systems, bring tangible innovations to enterprise operations, and serve as a reliable mentor and example for my siblings and anyone else trying to navigate their way forward without a pre-written guide.
      </p>
    </section>

